 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? It depends on the person. Many people learn it because the grammar is simple. But a lot also pick up Norwegian or Danish in school, so they' often fluent. Dutch and Danish are easy for Norwegians to understand, and the vocabulary often looks the same. It' a helpful thing for anyone learning the language. The pronunciation is often bit different from English. Some of the sounds are different, and some words written differently in writing. There's a big backlist of Dutch TV series, mostly about family life. There' also a lot of history and crime dramas, and a few science fiction series. Then you probably enjoy it. Many people start with the Dutch series and then switch to the original.",
